# Story page: pebble
# {name} becomes the snake's name. Paragraphs are separated by a blank line.
title = The Tortoise's Pebble
---
The old tortoise's lucky pebble, smooth as a promise and every bit as easy to lose.

He carried it for three hundred years and told everyone it was lucky. It was not lucky. He had simply never lost it, which is not the same thing, though people confuse the two constantly.

{name} kept it. The tortoise will never find out, because I have been sworn to secrecy, and I am, as you may have noticed, very bad at it.
